cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this code, cite the cloth-dynamics Lean tree it is vendored from.
title: cloth-dynamics Lean kernel emitters (vendored)
abstract: >-
  The lean/ tree of cloth-dynamics (TOOL_cloth_dynamics), added here as a
  squashed git subtree. Cloth.SlangCodegen.* builds 41 compute kernels as
  LeanSlang modules, among them the 24 AVBD kernels listed in
  kernels/avbd/kernels.txt (VBD init, gathers and solve/apply, the spring,
  attachment, membrane and bending forces with their augmented-Lagrangian
  dual updates, the self-collision scan and the ten backward kernels) that
  kernels/avbd/gen.sh compiles to cpp for AvbdCpu and to SPIR-V for AvbdRd;
  the rest are the PD/CG kernels (projections, saxpby, spmv, dot reductions,
  df32 variants). Cloth.Avbd.* states the AVBD specs (CSR
  adjacency, colouring, spring Hessian adjoint) with native_decide fixtures
  and plausible properties. lake exe emit_shaders writes every kernel's
  Slang; lake exe csr_falsify runs the plausible-witness-dag ladder over the
  CSR and colouring properties. Source commit e361584 is on branch
  feature/vulkan-avbd-windows-backend and not yet on any remote. Pins:
  lean-toolchain leanprover/lean4:v4.30.0; LeanSlang
  V-Sekai-fire/lean-slang v0.0.5 (813d6c62b298bcd3f7177264179a7e1d16bd87cd);
  plausible V-Sekai-fire/plausible v4.30.0
  (a456461b368b71d2accd95234832cd9c174b5437); plausible-witness-dag
  V-Sekai-fire/plausible-witness-dag
  160b94c9c6eed3bb9ebffce919fc6f989dcafba8. Adapted here: plausible and
  plausible-witness-dag are fetched from the V-Sekai-fire forks instead of
  leanprover-community/plausible and fire/plausible-witness-dag, and
  plausible-witness-dag is pinned by SHA instead of following main; the
  manifest revs are unchanged. No Lean source is modified.
type: software
